@page "/kilder"
@using Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Blazor
@using Fhi.Munin.Explorer.Contracts
@inject NavigationManager Nav

<PageTitle>Modern host — kilder</PageTitle>

<div class="hostchrome">
    <p class="hostchrome-note">
        The other root component the package ships: <code>KildeExplorer</code>, the
        kildeutforsker. <code>VariableExplorer</code> is on <a href="/">the front page</a> — the
        two are separate entry points, not two tabs of one thing, so each gets a page here.
    </p>
    <p class="hostchrome-note">
        <code>prerender: false</code> is not a preference on this page. <code>KildeExplorer</code>
        raises <code>SelectedKildeIdChanged</code>, and an <code>EventCallback</code> serialises to
        an empty delegate across a static-SSR to interactive-island boundary — the mount point has
        to be fully interactive or the callback silently never fires.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="hostframe">
    @* render-mode is set HERE, by the host. The component itself is render-mode free — the same
       arrangement as Home.razor, and for the same reason: prerendering would run the component's
       initialise-time fetch twice against the public API on every page load. *@
    <KildeExplorer Language="no"
                   ExploreVariablesRequested="ExploreVariables"
                   @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The handover out of Kelda, which is the host's to perform: the component says which kilder
    /// the reader chose, and only the host knows where it mounted a variable explorer.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The front page here, with the ids written as the query <c>VariableExplorer.Filter</c>
    /// already reads. The format is not restated: <c>VariableFilter.ToQueryString</c> writes what
    /// <c>VariableFilter.Parse</c> reads over there, so the two ends cannot drift apart. An empty
    /// list means the reader narrowed nothing, so it lands on the unfiltered list rather than on a
    /// query asking for no kilder at all.
    /// <para>
    /// This host has a router, so this is an ordinary in-app navigation — unlike LegacyHost, whose
    /// front page is an MVC view and has to force a load. The component itself is the same either
    /// way; what differs is the hosting model, which is the whole reason both samples are kept.
    /// </para>
    /// </remarks>
    private void ExploreVariables(IReadOnlyList<Guid> kildeIds)
    {
        var query = new VariableFilter { KildeIds = kildeIds }.ToQueryString();

        Nav.NavigateTo(query.Length == 0 ? "/" : "/?" + query);
    }
}
